\section{Caveats}{
\itemize{
\item Containment, not digestion: a protein contains a peptide if its sequence contains it anywhere, whatever the protease. Deliberately conservative.
\item Identical sequences under different accessions are one sequence: the peptide is Unique and lists both accessions.
\item Contaminants are searched; leaving the contaminant database out can turn a SharedAcrossGenes peptide (YLYEIAR, human and bovine albumin) into Unique.
\item A FASTA protein has no ensembl: key, so gene sharing for it rests on organism + primary gene name and the UniProt entry.
}
}
\section{Performance}{
Every call starts one bridge process, which costs a .NET start-up before any work. 
}
